To fix the issue where your Status screen incorrectly shows "Immediate Execution" despite the creator scheduling a time, you need to update the logic in your **VoucherPostingStatus.jsx** file.
The core of the problem is that your current code is trying to calculate the schedule status on the fly. We need to force it to read the **immutable history row** instead.
### 1. Update the workflowHistory.map logic in VoucherPostingStatus.jsx
Find the workflowHistory.map function. Replace the entire block starting from return ( inside the map with this fully updated version. This version uses the rawAction and the history.SCHEDULED_TIME snapshot to ensure the display is correct for both the Creator and the Approver.
```javascript
{workflowHistory.map((history, idx) => {
    const isSystem = history.LAST_ACTION_BY === "SYSTEM";
    const userName = history.ACTION_USER_NAME || (isSystem ? "Automated System" : "User");
    const initial = isSystem ? "S" : userName.charAt(0).toUpperCase();

    // 1. Clean the action label
    const rawAction = history.LAST_ACTION || "System Action";
    const cleanAction = rawAction.replace(/\s*\(.*?\)\s*/g, '').trim();

    // 2. Identify action types
    const isSubmission = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("SUBMIT");
    const isFinalApproval = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("FINAL") || rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("ACCEPT");
    
    // We look for our explicit flags
    const isSchOverride = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("SCH. OVERRIDE");
    const isImmOverride = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("IMM. OVERRIDE");
    const isKeptSchedule = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("(SCHEDULED)");

    // 3. STRICT HISTORICAL SNAPSHOT: Use the time logged for this specific event
    const historyRowTime = history.SCHEDULED_TIME;

    return (
        <Box key={idx} sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 2, mb: 2 }}>
            <Box>
                <Avatar sx={{ bgcolor: isSystem ? 'secondary.main' : 'primary.main', width: 40, height: 40, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>
                    {initial}
                </Avatar>
            </Box>
            <Box sx={{ flexGrow: 1, backgroundColor: "white", p: 2, borderRadius: 2, border: "1px solid #e2e8f0" }}>
                <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', gap: 1, mb: 1 }}>
                    <Typography variant="subtitle2" fontWeight="bold">{userName}</Typography>
                    <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">• {formatDateTime(history.LAST_ACTION_AT)}</Typography>
                </Box>
                
                <Stack direction="row" spacing={1} alignItems="center" sx={{ flexWrap: "wrap", gap: 1 }}>
                    <Chip label={cleanAction} size="small" />

                    {/* --- THE FIX: HISTORICAL LOGIC --- */}
                    {isSubmission && historyRowTime ? (
                        <Chip label={`Scheduled for: ${formatDateTime(historyRowTime)}`} size="small" color="info" variant="outlined" />
                    ) : isFinalApproval && !isSystem ? (
                        isSchOverride && historyRowTime ? (
                            <Chip label={`Schedule Overridden to: ${formatDateTime(historyRowTime)}`} size="small" color="warning" variant="outlined" />
                        ) : isImmOverride ? (
                            <Chip label="Overridden to Immediate Execution" size="small" color="warning" variant="outlined" />
                        ) : isKeptSchedule && historyRowTime ? (
                            <Chip label={`Original Schedule Kept: ${formatDateTime(historyRowTime)}`} size="small" color="info" variant="outlined" />
                        ) : (
                            <Chip label="Immediate Execution" size="small" color="default" variant="outlined" />
                        )
                    ) : isSubmission ? (
                        <Chip label="Immediate Execution" size="small" color="default" variant="outlined" />
                    ) : null}
                </Stack>
                <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ mt: 1 }}>{history.REMARKS}</Typography>
            </Box>
        </Box>
    );
})}

```
### 2. Why this solves your problem:
 * **Audit Trail Integrity:** By using historyRowTime = history.SCHEDULED_TIME, we are now reading the time that was saved in the database **at the exact moment the creator clicked "Submit."**
 * **Separation of Concerns:** Because this is inside the workflowHistory.map loop, it treats every action as its own event. Even if a Final Approver overrides the time 10 minutes later, the "Submitted" history row will **never change** because it is referencing its own dedicated snapshot in the VOUCHER_WORKFLOW table.
 * **No Overwriting:** It completely ignores the vidDetails.SCHEDULED_TIME (the current state) when rendering the history logs, so the Final Approver's actions will only appear on the "Final Approval" row, never on the "Submitted" row.
**Final Check:** Once you apply this code, your "TCS Maker" entry will show its own scheduled time, and the "Final Approval" entry will show its own rescheduling chip, and they will never clash.
